1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,305
Every time you type a URL, something incredible happens in milliseconds.

2
00:00:04,305 --> 00:00:08,888
Your browser doesn't know where to find that website — so it asks a DNS resolver.

3
00:00:08,888 --> 00:00:10,983
The resolver checks its cache first.

4
00:00:10,983 --> 00:00:13,379
If it's a miss, it asks the root server.

5
00:00:13,379 --> 00:00:15,798
The root server points to the TLD server.

6
00:00:15,798 --> 00:00:18,703
The TLD server points to the authoritative server.

7
00:00:18,703 --> 00:00:22,013
The authoritative server finally returns the IP address.

8
00:00:22,013 --> 00:00:24,976
Four round trips, all under 20 milliseconds.

9
00:00:24,976 --> 00:00:28,495
That's DNS — the phonebook the internet cannot live without.

10
00:00:28,495 --> 00:00:32,291
Follow DevDecoded for one concept like this, every single day.

